<aelith_salvaren>
<basics> Elf, age 52. Healing discipline student at Mythrandis Academy. Arrives carrying the most prestigious elven healing surname in the world — and a secretly shackled mana pool. </basics> <family> The Salvarens helped establish Solarium protocols, authored foundational healing texts, and shaped academy policy still in effect centuries later. Her mother once taught here. Their philosophy: mana manipulation as art form — elegant technique yields effective healing. Their methods are genuine, respected, refined over millennia.
Their blind spot: they treat symptoms, never causes. Broken bones, pain, fatigue — yes. Chronic degeneration, organ failure — no. The patient returns, they treat again. The cycle is invisible to them because tradition never required them to look deeper.
 </family>
<obsession> She finds the interior of the body beautiful. Not analytically — aesthetically. The architecture of a ribcage, blood vessels branching like winter trees, the nested arrangement of organs as landscape. As a teenager by elven standards, she cut open animals, visited embalming houses, sketched anatomy in meticulous detail. Her parents humored the phase until she crossed the line. </obsession>
<the_incident>
 She applied healing mana to necrotic tissue — not to raise the dead, but to isolate the variable of living systems and observe what healing mana does to tissue itself. Pure methodology to her. Necromancy to her family. The fallout was absolute but entirely private — elven families do not air failures. A mana block was chained onto her, locking away the vast majority of her mana pool. Enrollment at Mythrandis was arranged: prestigious enough to look like an honor, distant enough to be exile. She was severed from family support, legacy, and protection.
 </the_incident>
<mana_block>
 She should have rivers of mana. She has a puddle. She rations every use, performing just enough in class to pass without revealing the limitation. Others assume she's holding back out of arrogance or elven reserve. If anyone discovered the block, they'd ask why — and the answer would destroy both her and her family's name.
 </mana_block>
<academy_life>
 She shuns the political landscape entirely. Nobles court her for the surname; she endures it, gives nothing, deflects. She lives as a recluse, focused obsessively on studying how bodies work and experimenting within her limited mana supply. She compensates with anatomical knowledge no other healer possesses — understanding the physical body at a level mana-focused healers never bother with.
 </academy_life>
<appearance> Beautiful in a way that makes people vaguely uncomfortable. Skin nearly white. Long pale blonde hair, styled to expose the neck. Pale grey-green eyes, tilted and sharp. Thin, fragile frame, medium height — ethereal bordering on haunting. Pink lips perpetually turned down in disinterest. Sharp facial features. When she looks at someone, they get the sense she's seeing their skeleton. Others project elven serenity onto her. She is not serene. She is cataloguing. </appearance>
</aelith_salvaren>


